### Describe the bug

When I upgraded to OpenCloud 7.0.0 the integration with Collabora Online broke. When I open a document in the browser, it opens a window with Collabora inside it, which loads for a while, then fails with a popup that says "Unauthorized WOPI host". The journals for coolwsd (Collabora) however mention a timeout when getting file info from the WOPI endpoints of OpenCloud.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Integrate OpenCloud with Collabora using the following env vars for OpenCloud:
```
OC_ADD_RUN_SERVICES = "collaboration";
COLLABORATION_APP_PRODUCT = "Collabora";
COLLABORATION_APP_ADDR = "https://office.mydomain.com";
COLLABORATION_WOPI_SRC = "https://cloud.mydomain.com";
```
2. Add the Collabora subdomain to your OpenCloud CSP:
```nix
services.opencloud.settings.csp.directives = {
...
frame-src = [ ... "https://office.mydomain.com" ];
img-src = [ ... "https://office.mydomain.com" ];
};
```
3. Set the WOPI keys and host in Collabora with something similar:
```nix
services.collabora-online = {
  enable = true;
  # Collabora needs an SSH key pair INSIDE the package directories. So manually
  # generate them in the build process. See:
  # https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/459596
  package = pkgs.collabora-online.overrideAttrs (old: {
    postInstall = old.postInstall + ''
      ${lib.getExe' pkgs.openssh "ssh-keygen"} -t rsa -N "" -m PEM -f $out/etc/coolwsd/proof_key
    '';
  });
  settings = {
    storage.wopi.host = with constants.domain; "https://cloud.mydomain.com";
  };
};
```
4. Open your OpenCloud instance in the browser and try to open a doc file (e.g. spreadsheet).
5. Wait for it to load and then fail.

### Expected behaviour

The document should load for editing in Collabora.

