#290052 changed this package to fetch the font file from the [google/fonts](https://github.com/google/fonts) repository, to get a variable font and avoid the API token requirement.

However, it seems the version in the github repo is not up to date with the version served from google fonts. See https://github.com/google/fonts/issues/7937.

Anyways, I believe I've found a way to get this font from google webfonts in variable form, without needing an API key — using the css interface:
```
[user@hostname ~]$ curl 'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Noto+Emoji'
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Noto Emoji';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  src: url(https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/notoemoji/v62/bMrnmSyK7YY-MEu6aWjPDs-ar6uWaGWuob-r0jwv.ttf) format('truetype');
}
```

So it should be pretty simple to make an updater script based on that.

